  "limits": [
    "Both baseline and candidate use installed native clients and retained Python workers with identical dependencies.",
    "Windows 11 / CPython 3.14, synthetic 250 modules x 12 methods; timings vary with machine load and are not latency guarantees.",
    "Seven final samples per scenario, alternating execution order; nearest-rank p95 equals maximum. All fifteen-sample earlier controls are retained separately.",
    "CLI includes native startup, IPC, fresh Git capture, analysis and JSON output; worker/cache initialization is separate.",
    "The normal staged prek and pre-commit hooks include runner startup and their single Smelt hook; installation and other hooks are excluded.",
    "Each edited report matches an independent fresh-process --no-cache report. Hook comparisons use separate repositories/caches.",
    "The candidate combines verified policy blob reuse, a persistent Rust Git reader and bounded retained member dependency state.",
    "Default cached staged checks use the native reader without Git child processes; --base resolution, unsupported repositories, overrides other than GIT_INDEX_FILE, and --no-cache retain the independent Git path.",
    "The helper starts once per Python process and drops repository handles after each operation. HEAD and the complete current index are recaptured on every check.",
    "The worker retains at most two member dependency snapshots with an 8 MiB serialized-content budget. Inputs are compared on every use, and failed mutations relinquish the borrowed snapshot.",
    "No universal or cold-CI speedup is claimed. Normal working-tree CI checks stay in the foreground; retained dependency state is worker-only.",
    "Unaccepted worker requests fall back after 250 ms. Accepted responses have a five-second absolute budget; partial bytes cannot prolong it. Foreground checking time is additional.",
    "Workers use a five-second self-exit watchdog and at most four OS-owned slots per cache directory. A saturated pool uses foreground checking; a crash releases its lock.",
    "Full CLI/hook and memory measurements use 81dbcfa. The final 03f3171 change only prevents a repeated worker attempt after an accepted transport failure; the same Python package and successful path are checked in the separate final_path_control."
  ],
